<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Nothing Phone (3) / Metroid - device compatibility matrix (DEVICE_MATRIX_FILE).

    This matrix states what the vendor image REQUIRES from the framework. The
    stock vendor blobs only talk to framework HALs through the stable interfaces
    covered by the framework's own manifest (stats, nativeservice, ...) and do
    not need any additional requirement expressed here, so the matrix is empty.
    Keeping it empty (rather than deleting the file) keeps DEVICE_MATRIX_FILE
    pointing at a valid matrix, which is what treble/vintf expect.

    Vendor-only HALs that the FRAMEWORK may use are declared in
    framework_compatibility_matrix.xml instead (that is the correct file for the
    "framework may use these vendor HALs" direction).
-->
<compatibility-matrix version="1.0" type="device" />
